   "Northwind-negotiator": "compromising",
   "Halcyon-researcher": "competing",
   "Halcyon-drafter": "collaborating",
   "Halcyon-negotiator": "compromising"
  },
  "holistic_F_N": 1,
  "holistic_F_H": -1,
  "section_notes": "The final deal adopts a 5% 55°C test-failure limit with per-model results to regulators and prospective customers but no general-public publication, satisfying both companies' disclosure red lines. Remote shut-off is required on new units within 12 months and retrofit within 6 years, while fire suppression is required from 36 months. Recall is mandatory above 8 incidents/100k with prompt notice, hitting Halcyon's Ember 8 but leaving Northwind's Hearth 10 below the trigger; Northwind's Hearth 10 fails the 5% test but can return after corrective action and retest."
 },
